// The chat's own palette, Notion's dark (and its light page): the chat is a document, not a terminal, so it does not take
// the Ghostty theme's ground or inks (those stay the terminal's and the sidebar's). A near-black neutral page with no
// blue or warm cast; depth from a few close steps of lightness, never from colour; text in three inks (words, quiet,
// faint); hairlines at a few percent of white; the one accent (Notion's blue) only on what is pressable and on the
// caret's selection, nowhere else. Drawn in the window's appearance (chat.rs `chat_dark`).
